n\n$4p^2/9 = 144$\n\n$p^2 = 324$\n\n$p = 18$ (positive).\n\nSo $q = 225/18 = 12.5 = 25/2$.\n\n$u = (18 + 81/18)/2 = (18 + 4.5)/2 = 22.5/2 = 11.25 = 45/4$.\n\nWait let me recompute: $u = (p + 81/p)/2 = (18 + 81/18)/2 = (18 + 4.5)/2 = 22.5/2 = 11.25 = 45/4$.\n\n$v = (p - 81/p)/2 = (18 - 4.5)/2 = 13.5/2 = 6.75 = 27/4$.\n\nCheck: $u^2 = 2025/16$, $v^2 = 729/16$, $u^2 - v^2 = 1296/16 = 81$. ✓\n\n$w = (q - 125/q)/2 = (25/2 - 125/(25/2))/2 = (25/2 - 125 \\cdot 2/25)/2 = (25/2 - 10)/2 = (25/2 - 20/2)/2 = (5/2)/2 = 5/4$.\n\nCheck: $w^2 = 25/16$, $v^2 - w^2 = 729/16 - 25/16 = 704/16 = 44$. ✓\n\n$u^2 - w^2 = 2025/16 - 25/16 = 2000/16 = 125$. ✓\n\nNow $t = 225 - u^2 = 225 - 2025/16 = (3600 - 2025)/16 = 1575/16$.\n\nCheck $t = 100 - w^2 = 100 - 25/16 = (1600-25)/16 = 1575/16$. ✓\n\nNow $\\alpha^2 = \\frac{7t}{225-t} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 1575/16}{225 - 1575/16} = \\frac{11025/16}{(3600-1575)/16} = \\frac{11025}{2025} = \\frac{11025}{2025}$.\n\nSimplify: $\\gcd(11025, 2025)$. $11025 = 5 \\cdot 2205 = 5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 441 = 25 \\cdot 441 = 25 \\cdot 21^2 = 25 \\cdot 441$. $2025 = 25 \\cdot 81 = 25 \\cdot 81$. So $\\frac{11025}{2025} = \\frac{441}{81} = \\frac{49}{9}$.\n\nSo $\\alpha^2 = 49/9$, $\\alpha = 7/3$.\n\n$\\beta^2 = \\frac{7t}{144-t} = \\frac{11025/16}{(2304-1575)/16} = \\frac{11025}{729}$. $11025 = 25 \\cdot 441$, $729 = 729$. $\\gcd$: $11025/729$... $729 = 3^6 = 729$. $11025 = 3^2 \\cdot 1225 = 9 \\cdot 1225$. $1225 = 25 \\cdot 49$. So $11025 = 9 \\cdot 25 \\cdot 49 = 9 \\cdot 1225$. $729 = 9 \\cdot 81$. So $\\frac{11025}{729} = \\frac{1225}{81}$. $\\beta = 35/9$.\n\n$\\gamma^2 = \\frac{7t}{100-t} = \\frac{11025/16}{(1600-1575)/16} = \\frac{11025}{25} = 441$. $\\gamma = 21$.\n\nLet me verify the equilibrium: $\\frac{225 \\cdot 49/9}{49/9 + 7} = \\frac{225 \\cdot 49/9}{(49+63)/9} = \\frac{225 \\cdot 49/9}{112/9} = \\frac{225 \\cdot 49}{112} = \\frac{11025}{112}$.\n\n$\\frac{144 \\cdot 1225/81}{1225/81 + 7} = \\frac{144 \\cdot 1225/81}{(1225+567)/81} = \\frac{144 \\cdot 1225/81}{1792/81} = \\frac{144 \\cdot 1225}{1792} = \\frac{176400}{1792}$.\n\n$176400/1792$: divide by 16: $11025/112$. ✓ Same.\n\n$\\frac{100 \\cdot 441}{441+7} = \\frac{44100}{448} = \\frac{44100}{448}$. Divide by 4: $11025/112$. ✓\n\nNow Vieta's: $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 7/3 + 35/9 + 21 = 21/9 + 35/9 + 189/9 = 245/9$.\n\n$\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = (7/3)(35/9)(21) = 7 \\cdot 35 \\cdot 21 / 27 = 7 \\cdot 35 \\cdot 21/27$. $35 \\cdot 21 = 735$. $7 \\cdot 735 = 5145$. $5145/27 = 191.66...$. Let me compute: $5145/27 = 190.555...$. Hmm, $27 \\cdot 190 = 5130$, $5145-5130=15$, so $190 + 15/27 = 190 + 5/9 = 1715/9$.\n\nCheck: $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma) = 7 \\cdot 245/9 = 1715/9$. ✓\n\nNow $\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = (7/3)(35/9) + (35/9)(21) + (21)(7/3) = 245/27 + 735/9 + 147/3 = 245/27 + 2205/27 + 1323/27 = (245+2205+1323)/27 = 3773/27$.\n\nLet me recompute: $245 + 2205 = 2450$, $2450 + 1323 = 3773$. So $3773/27$.\n\nCheck if reducible: $3773 = 27 \\cdot 139 + 20$... $27 \\cdot 139 = 3753$, $3773 - 3753 = 20$. So $3773/27$ is irreducible (since $\\gcd(3773, 27)$: $3773 = 27 \\cdot 139 + 20$, $27 = 20 \\cdot 1 + 7$, $20 = 7 \\cdot 2 + 6$, $7 = 6 \\cdot 1 + 1$, so $\\gcd = 1$). Irreducible.\n\nNow $a_1/a_3 = \\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = 3773/27$.\n$1/a_3 = \\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma = 245/9$, so $a_3 = 9/245$.\n\n$a_1 = a_3 \\cdot 3773/27 = (9/245)(3773/27) = 9 \\cdot 3773/(245 \\cdot 27) = 3773/(245 \\cdot 3) = 3773/735$.\n\nCheck reducibility: $735 = 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7^2 = 735$. $3773 / 7 = 539$, $539/7 = 77$, so $3773 = 7 \\cdot 539 = 7 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 77 = 49 \\cdot 77 = 49 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11 = 343 \\cdot 11$. So $3773 = 7^3 \\cdot 11 = 343 \\cdot 11 = 3773$. \n\n$735 = 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7^2$. $3773 = 7^3 \\cdot 11$. $\\gcd = 7^2 = 49$.\n\n$a_1 = 3773/735 = (3773/49)/(735/49) = 77/15$.\n\nCheck: $3773/49 = 77$, $735/49 = 15$. So $a_1 = 77/15$.\n\n$\\gcd(77, 15) = 1$ (since $77 = 7 \\cdot 11$, $15 = 3 \\cdot 5$