{"type": "step", "node_id": 28, "parent_node_id": 26, "role": "assistant", "content": "## Solution\n\n**Setting up Vieta's relations.** The cubic $a_3 x^3 - x^2 + a_1 x - 7 = 0$ has positive roots $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma$, so by Vieta's:\n- $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 1/a_3$\n- $\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = a_1/a_3$\n- $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7/a_3$\n\nIn particular, $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)$.\n\n**Parameterizing the equilibrium condition.** Let the common value be $t$:\n$$\\frac{225\\alpha^2}{\\alpha^2+7} = \\frac{144\\beta^2}{\\beta^2+7} = \\frac{100\\gamma^2}{\\gamma^2+7} = t$$\n\nSolving each: $\\alpha^2 = \\frac{7t}{225-t}$, $\\beta^2 = \\frac{7t}{144-t}$, $\\gamma^2 = \\frac{7t}{100-t}$.\n\n**Substituting into $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)$.** Setting $u=\\sqrt{225-t},\\ v=\\sqrt{144-t},\\ w=\\sqrt{100-t}$ and dividing through by $\\sqrt{7t}$:\n\n$$\\frac{t}{uvw} = \\frac{1}{u}+\\frac{1}{v}+\\frac{1}{w} \\implies t = uv+vw+wu$$\n\nSince $t = 225 - u^2$: $u^2 + uv + vw + wu = 225$, which factors as $(u+v)(u+w) = 225$.\n\n**Using the differences.** Note $u^2-v^2=81$ and $u^2-w^2=125$, so $(u-v)(u+v)=81$ and $(u-w)(u+w)=125$.\n\nLet $p = u+v$, $q = u+w$, with $pq = 225$. Then $u-v = 81/p$ and $u-w = 125/q$, giving:\n$$u = \\tfrac{1}{2}(p + 81/p) = \\tfrac{1}{2}(q + 125/q), \\quad q = 225/p$$\n\nSubstituting: $p + 81/p = 225/p + 5p/9$, so $4p/9 = 144/p$, giving $p^2 = 324$, hence $p = 18$ and $q = 25/2$.\n\n**Computing the roots.**\n- $u = (18 + 4.5)/2 = 45/4$, so $t = 225 - 2025/16 = 1575/16$\n- $\\alpha^2 = \\frac{7 \\cdot 1575/16}{2025/16} = \\frac{11025}{2025} = \\frac{49}{9}$, so $\\alpha = 7/3$\n- $\\beta^2 = \\frac{11025/16}{729/16} = \\frac{1225}{81}$, so $\\beta = 35/9$\n- $\\gamma^2 = \\frac{11025/16}{25/16} = 441$, so $\\gamma = 21$\n\n**Verification of equilibrium:** All three ratios equal $11025/112$. ✓\n\n**Verification in the cubic:** Direct substitution confirms $x = 7/3,\\ 35/9,\\ 21$ each give $0$. ✓\n\n**Computing $a_1$.**\n$$\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = \\frac{245}{27} + \\frac{2205}{27} + \\frac{1323}{27} = \\frac{3773}{27}$$\n\n$$\\frac{1}{a_3} = \\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma = \\frac{245}{9} \\implies a_3 = \\frac{9}{245}$$\n\n$$a_1 = a_3 \\cdot \\frac{3773}{27} = \\frac{9}{245}\\cdot\\frac{3773}{27} = \\frac{3773}{735}$$\n\nFactoring: $3773 = 7^3 \\cdot 11$ and $735 = 3\\cdot 5\\cdot 7^2$, so $\\gcd = 49$:\n$$a_1 = \\frac{77}{15}, \\quad \\gcd(77,15)=1$$\n\nThe irreducible fraction is $a/b = 77/15$, so:\n\n$$a + b = 77 + 15 = \\boxed{92}$$\n\n### PROOF COMPLETE", "thinking": "Let me solve this problem. The cubic is $a_3 x^3 - x^2 + a_1 x - 7 = 0$ with positive real roots $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma$.\n\nBy Vieta's:\n- $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 1/a_3$\n- $\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = a_1/a_3$\n- $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7/a_3$\n\nThe equilibrium condition: $\\frac{225\\alpha^2}{\\alpha^2+7} = \\frac{144\\beta^2}{\\beta^2+7} = \\frac{100\\gamma^2}{\\gamma^2+7} = k$ (some constant).\n\nSo $\\frac{225\\alpha^2}{\\alpha^2+7} = k$, giving $225\\alpha^2 = k(\\alpha^2+7)$, so $\\alpha^2(225-k) = 7k$, thus $\\alpha^2 = \\frac{7k}{225-k}$.\n\nSimilarly $\\beta^2 = \\frac{7k}{144-k}$, $\\gamma^2 = \\frac{7k}{100-k}$.\n\nNow since $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma$ are roots of the cubic, and $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7/a_3$.\n\nLet me think about the structure. The numbers 225, 144, 100 are $15^2, 12^2, 10^2$. So let's write the common value as $k$.\n\nActually, let me think differently. Let $f(x) = \\frac{cx^2}{x^2+7}$ where $c$ is 225, 144, 100 for $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma$.\n\nNote that $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7/a_3$ and $\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma = 1/a_3$, so $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)$.\n\nHmm, let me think about this. We have $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)$.\n\nLet me set $t = k$. Then $\\alpha^2 = \\frac{7t}{225-t}$, etc.\n\nWe need $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma > 0$ so $t < 100$ (the smallest denominator constant) and $t > 0$.\n\nNow $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)$.\n\n$\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = \\sqrt{\\frac{7t}{225-t} \\cdot \\frac{7t}{144-t} \\cdot \\frac{7t}{100-t}} = (7t)^{3/2} / \\sqrt{(225-t)(144-t)(100-t)}$\n\n$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma = \\sqrt{\\frac{7t}{225-t}} + \\sqrt{\\frac{7t}{144-t}} + \\sqrt{\\frac{7t}{100-t}}$\n\n$= \\sqrt{7t}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{225-t}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{144-t}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{100-t}}\\right)$\n\nSo the condition $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)$ becomes:\n\n$(7t)^{3/2} / \\sqrt{(225-t)(144-t)(100-t)} = 7\\sqrt{7t}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{225-t}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{144-t}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{100-t}}\\right)$\n\nDivide both sides by $\\sqrt{7t}$:\n\n$7t / \\sqrt{(225-t)(144-t)(100-t)} = 7\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{225-t}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{144-t}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{100-t}}\\right)$\n\n$t / \\sqrt{(225-t)(144-t)(100-t)} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{225-t}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{144-t}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{100-t}}$\n\nLet $u = \\sqrt{225-t}$, $v = \\sqrt{144-t}$, $w = \\sqrt{100-t}$. Note $u^2 - v^2 = 81$, $v^2 - w^2 = 44$, $u^2 - w^2 = 125$.\n\n$t = 225 - u^2 = 144 - v^2 = 100 - w^2$.\n\nThe equation: $\\frac{t}{uvw} = \\frac{1}{u} + \\frac{1}{v} + \\frac{1}{w} = \\frac{vw + uw + uv}{uvw}$\n\nSo $t = vw + uw + uv = uv + vw + wu$.\n\nSo $225 - u^2 = uv + vw + wu$, i.e., $u^2 + uv + vw + wu = 225$.\n\n$u^2 + uv + vw + wu = u(u+v) + w(u+v) = (u+w)(u+v) = 225$.\n\nSo $(u+v)(u+w) = 225$.\n\nAlso $u^2 - v^2 = 81 \\Rightarrow (u-v)(u+v) = 81$.\nAnd $u^2 - w^2 = 125 \\Rightarrow (u-w)(u+w) = 125$.\n\nLet $p = u+v$, $q = u+w$. Then $pq = 225$.\n$u - v = 81/p$, so $u = (p + 81/p)/2$, $v = (p - 81/p)/2$.\n$u - w = 125/q$, so $u = (q + 125/q)/2$, $w = (q - 125/q)/2$.\n\nFrom $u$: $(p + 81/p)/2 = (q + 125/q)/2$, so $p + 81/p = q + 125/q$.\n\nAnd $pq = 225$, so $q = 225/p$.\n\n$p + 81/p = 225/p + 125p/225 = 225/p + 5p/9$.\n\n$p + 81/p = 5p/9 + 225/p$\n\n$p - 5p/9 = 225/p - 81/p$\n\n$4p/9 = 144/p$\n\n$4p^2/9 = 144$\n\n$p^2 = 324$\n\n$p = 18$ (positive).\n\nSo $q = 225/18 = 12.5 = 25/2$.\n\n$u = (18 + 81/18)/2 = (18 + 4.5)/2 = 22.5/2 = 11.25 = 45/4$.\n\nWait let me recompute: $u = (p + 81/p)/2 = (18 + 81/18)/2 = (18 + 4.5)/2 = 22.5/2 = 11.25 = 45/4$.\n\n$v = (p - 81/p)/2 = (18 - 4.5)/2 = 13.5/2 = 6.75 = 27/4$.\n\nCheck: $u^2 = 2025/16$, $v^2 = 729/16$, $u^2 - v^2 = 1296/16 = 81$. ✓\n\n$w = (q - 125/q)/2 = (25/2 - 125/(25/2))/2 = (25/2 - 125 \\cdot 2/25)/2 = (25/2 - 10)/2 = (25/2 - 20/2)/2 = (5/2)/2 = 5/4$.\n\nCheck: $w^2 = 25/16$, $v^2 - w^2 = 729/16 - 25/16 = 704/16 = 44$. ✓\n\n$u^2 - w^2 = 2025/16 - 25/16 = 2000/16 = 125$. ✓\n\nNow $t = 225 - u^2 = 225 - 2025/16 = (3600 - 2025)/16 = 1575/16$.\n\nCheck $t = 100 - w^2 = 100 - 25/16 = (1600-25)/16 = 1575/16$. ✓\n\nNow $\\alpha^2 = \\frac{7t}{225-t} = \\frac{7 \\cdot 1575/16}{225 - 1575/16} = \\frac{11025/16}{(3600-1575)/16} = \\frac{11025}{2025} = \\frac{11025}{2025}$.\n\nSimplify: $\\gcd(11025, 2025)$. $11025 = 5 \\cdot 2205 = 5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 441 = 25 \\cdot 441 = 25 \\cdot 21^2 = 25 \\cdot 441$. $2025 = 25 \\cdot 81 = 25 \\cdot 81$. So $\\frac{11025}{2025} = \\frac{441}{81} = \\frac{49}{9}$.\n\nSo $\\alpha^2 = 49/9$, $\\alpha = 7/3$.\n\n$\\beta^2 = \\frac{7t}{144-t} = \\frac{11025/16}{(2304-1575)/16} = \\frac{11025}{729}$. $11025 = 25 \\cdot 441$, $729 = 729$. $\\gcd$: $11025/729$... $729 = 3^6 = 729$. $11025 = 3^2 \\cdot 1225 = 9 \\cdot 1225$. $1225 = 25 \\cdot 49$. So $11025 = 9 \\cdot 25 \\cdot 49 = 9 \\cdot 1225$. $729 = 9 \\cdot 81$. So $\\frac{11025}{729} = \\frac{1225}{81}$. $\\beta = 35/9$.\n\n$\\gamma^2 = \\frac{7t}{100-t} = \\frac{11025/16}{(1600-1575)/16} = \\frac{11025}{25} = 441$. $\\gamma = 21$.\n\nLet me verify the equilibrium: $\\frac{225 \\cdot 49/9}{49/9 + 7} = \\frac{225 \\cdot 49/9}{(49+63)/9} = \\frac{225 \\cdot 49/9}{112/9} = \\frac{225 \\cdot 49}{112} = \\frac{11025}{112}$.\n\n$\\frac{144 \\cdot 1225/81}{1225/81 + 7} = \\frac{144 \\cdot 1225/81}{(1225+567)/81} = \\frac{144 \\cdot 1225/81}{1792/81} = \\frac{144 \\cdot 1225}{1792} = \\frac{176400}{1792}$.\n\n$176400/1792$: divide by 16: $11025/112$. ✓ Same.\n\n$\\frac{100 \\cdot 441}{441+7} = \\frac{44100}{448} = \\frac{44100}{448}$. Divide by 4: $11025/112$. ✓\n\nNow Vieta's: $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 7/3 + 35/9 + 21 = 21/9 + 35/9 + 189/9 = 245/9$.\n\n$\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = (7/3)(35/9)(21) = 7 \\cdot 35 \\cdot 21 / 27 = 7 \\cdot 35 \\cdot 21/27$. $35 \\cdot 21 = 735$. $7 \\cdot 735 = 5145$. $5145/27 = 191.66...$. Let me compute: $5145/27 = 190.555...$. Hmm, $27 \\cdot 190 = 5130$, $5145-5130=15$, so $190 + 15/27 = 190 + 5/9 = 1715/9$.\n\nCheck: $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = 7(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma) = 7 \\cdot 245/9 = 1715/9$. ✓\n\nNow $\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = (7/3)(35/9) + (35/9)(21) + (21)(7/3) = 245/27 + 735/9 + 147/3 = 245/27 + 2205/27 + 1323/27 = (245+2205+1323)/27 = 3773/27$.\n\nLet me recompute: $245 + 2205 = 2450$, $2450 + 1323 = 3773$. So $3773/27$.\n\nCheck if reducible: $3773 = 27 \\cdot 139 + 20$... $27 \\cdot 139 = 3753$, $3773 - 3753 = 20$. So $3773/27$ is irreducible (since $\\gcd(3773, 27)$: $3773 = 27 \\cdot 139 + 20$, $27 = 20 \\cdot 1 + 7$, $20 = 7 \\cdot 2 + 6$, $7 = 6 \\cdot 1 + 1$, so $\\gcd = 1$). Irreducible.\n\nNow $a_1/a_3 = \\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = 3773/27$.\n$1/a_3 = \\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma = 245/9$, so $a_3 = 9/245$.\n\n$a_1 = a_3 \\cdot 3773/27 = (9/245)(3773/27) = 9 \\cdot 3773/(245 \\cdot 27) = 3773/(245 \\cdot 3) = 3773/735$.\n\nCheck reducibility: $735 = 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7^2 = 735$. $3773 / 7 = 539$, $539/7 = 77$, so $3773 = 7 \\cdot 539 = 7 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 77 = 49 \\cdot 77 = 49 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11 = 343 \\cdot 11$. So $3773 = 7^3 \\cdot 11 = 343 \\cdot 11 = 3773$. \n\n$735 = 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7^2$. $3773 = 7^3 \\cdot 11$. $\\gcd = 7^2 = 49$.\n\n$a_1 = 3773/735 = (3773/49)/(735/49) = 77/15$.\n\nCheck: $3773/49 = 77$, $735/49 = 15$. So $a_1 = 77/15$.\n\n$\\gcd(77, 15) = 1$ (since $77 = 7 \\cdot 11$, $15 = 3 \\cdot 5$). Irreducible.\n\nSo $a + b = 77 + 15 = 92$.\n\nLet me double-check the whole computation once more.\n\n$\\alpha = 7/3, \\beta = 35/9, \\gamma = 21$.\n\n$\\alpha\\beta = (7/3)(35/9) = 245/27$.\n$\\beta\\gamma = (35/9)(21) = 735/9 = 2205/27$.\n$\\gamma\\alpha = (21)(7/3) = 147/3 = 1323/27$.\n\nSum $= (245 + 2205 + 1323)/27 = 3773/27$.\n\n$a_3 = 9/245$, $a_1 = (9/245)(3773/27) = 3773/(245 \\cdot 3) = 3773/735$.\n\n$3773 = 7^3 \\cdot 11$, $735 = 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7^2$. $\\gcd = 49$. $a_1 = 77/15$.\n\n$a + b = 92$.\n\nLet me verify the cubic: $a_3 x^3 - x^2 + a_1 x - 7 = (9/245)x^3 - x^2 + (77/15)x - 7$.\n\nCheck $x = 7/3$: $(9/245)(343/27) - 49/9 + (77/15)(7/3) - 7 = (9 \\cdot 343)/(245 \\cdot 27) - 49/9 + 539/45 - 7$.\n\n$9 \\cdot 343 = 3087$, $245 \\cdot 27 = 6615$, $3087/6615 = 3087/6615$. Divide by 9: $343/735 = 343/735$. Divide by 49: $7/15$.\n\nSo first term $= 7/15$.\n\n$-49/9 + 539/45 - 7$. Common denominator 45: $-245/45 + 539/45 - 315/45 = (-245 + 539 - 315)/45 = (-21)/45 = -7/15$.\n\nTotal: $7/15 - 7/15 = 0$. ✓\n\nCheck $x = 21$: $(9/245)(9261) - 441 + (77/15)(21) - 7 = 9 \\cdot 9261/245 - 441 + 1617/15 - 7$.\n\n$9 \\cdot 9261 = 83349$, $83349/245 = 340$. $245 \\cdot 340 = 83300$, $83349 - 83300 = 49$, so $340 + 49/245 = 340 + 1/5 = 1701/5$.\n\n$1617/15 = 107.8 = 539/5$.\n\n$1701/5 - 441 + 539/5 - 7 = (1701+539)/5 - 448 = 2240/5 - 448 = 448 - 448 = 0$. ✓\n\nCheck $x = 35/9$: $(9/245)(35/9)^3 - (35/9)^2 + (77/15)(35/9) - 7$.\n\n$(35/9)^3 = 42875/729$. $(9/245)(42875/729) = 9 \\cdot 42875/(245 \\cdot 729) = 42875/(245 \\cdot 81) = 42875/19845$. \n\n$42875 = 5^3 \\cdot 7^3 = 125 \\cdot 343 = 42875$. $19845 = 245 \\cdot 81 = 5 \\cdot 49 \\cdot 81 = 5 \\cdot 3969 = 19845$. $\\gcd$: $42875 = 5^3 \\cdot 7^3$, $19845 = 5 \\cdot 7^2 \\cdot 3^4$. $\\gcd = 5 \\cdot 7^2 = 245$. $42875/245 = 175$, $19845/245 = 81$. So first term $= 175/81$.\n\n$(35/9)^2 = 1225/81$. \n\n$(77/15)(35/9) = 2695/135 = 539/27 = 1617/81$.\n\n$175/81 - 1225/81 + 1617/81 - 7 = (175 - 1225 + 1617)/81 - 7 = 567/81 - 7 = 7 - 7 = 0$. ✓\n\nAll three roots check out. The answer is $a_1 = 77/15$, and $a + b = 77 + 15 = 92$.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1787225511}
